    <h1>Protecting Your Internet Connection While Travelling</h1>
    <p class="article-intro">When travelling, you connect your phone and laptop to Wi-Fi networks you don't control. Hotels, airports, cafés, coworking spaces — these networks are convenient, but they expose your connection to real risks.</p>

    <h2>Why Public Wi-Fi Is Risky</h2>
    <p>An unsecured public Wi-Fi network allows anyone on the same network to intercept your traffic. This isn't theoretical — it's a simple technique accessible to anyone with basic equipment.</p>
    <p>What can be intercepted on an unsecured Wi-Fi:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your credentials on sites without HTTPS</li>
      <li>Session cookies — which can allow someone to log in as you on certain services</li>
      <li>Your emails if you use an unencrypted mail client</li>
      <li>Data you submit through unsecured forms</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What a VPN Actually Changes</h2>
    <p>When you activate VulcainVPN, all your traffic is <strong>encrypted before leaving your device</strong>. Even if someone intercepts data on the hotel Wi-Fi, they only see an unreadable encrypted stream.</p>
    <p>Encryption works across all your simultaneously connected devices — phone, laptop, tablet — under a single subscription.</p>

    <div class="article-highlight">
      <h3>In Practice While Travelling</h3>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>Hotel Wi-Fi</strong> — activate the VPN as soon as you connect, before opening email or banking</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>Airport</strong> — airport networks are among the most targeted, VPN is especially useful here</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>Café / coworking</strong> — same logic, shared network with strangers</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> <strong>Local SIM card</strong> — even on mobile data, the VPN encrypts your traffic from the local operator</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Multiple Protocols for Your Situation</h2>
    <p>VulcainVPN offers three connection protocols:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>WireGuard</strong> — the fastest, ideal for normal connections while travelling in Europe</li>
      <li><strong>Hysteria2</strong> — designed for high-latency or unstable networks (satellite connection, congested network)</li>
      <li><strong>Shadowsocks</strong> — useful on networks that filter or throttle standard VPN connections</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The app automatically selects the best protocol based on your network.</p>

    <h2>Available on Android and Windows</h2>
